  "notes": "A godan verb describing the forceful ejection of liquid, gas, or lava. Distinguished from the homophone {吹|ふ}く (to blow) by focusing on liquid or molten substances rather than air or wind.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Both ({自動詞|じどうし} and {他動詞|たどうし})\n- Intransitive: {水|みず}が{噴|ふ}く (water gushes)\n- Transitive: {潮|しお}を{噴|ふ}く (to spout water)\n\nASPECT:\n- {噴|ふ}いている: is currently spouting/erupting (ongoing action)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {潮|しお}を{噴|ふ}く: to spout water (whales)\n- {蒸気|じょうき}を{噴|ふ}く: to vent steam\n- {火|ひ}を{噴|ふ}く: to spew fire\n- {噴|ふ}き{出|だ}す: to gush out, to spew forth (compound verb)\n- {噴|ふ}き{上|あ}げる: to spout upward\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {吹|ふ}く: to blow — used for wind, breath, and musical instruments; never for liquids\n- {噴出|ふんしゅつ}する: to erupt, to gush — more formal and used in scientific or news contexts",
